From c0aa6f07e6bf4bf29f97893bdf554646c0d1f877 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stew Forster <stew675@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 21:37:36 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 14/28] WIP GDN/PLE: port the depthwise conv1d prefill fusions

Phase-1 item 2 of wip/closing-the-gap.  Ports the other solution's
ggml/src/ggml-cuda/gdn-conv.cu + ple-conv.cu (and their .cuh) into the
delivery: a direct kernel reads the recurrent state + x and writes the conv
output (+ silu), replacing the CONCAT(state, x) materialization and the
SSM_CONV / tap-mul-add-silu chain.  The CONCAT is still partially
materialized for the recurrent snapshot copies (its tail only).

Only two adaptations were needed for our tree:
* grouped_norm emits a 3-D [n_embd, hc, T] MUL (the 2026-09-15 re-base) whose
  view root is the transpose's view_src, so ple_conv_check derives C/T from the
  transpose and only requires the root to be a contiguous F32 buffer of C*T.
* the shared build_conv_state (qwen35moe/qwen35/qwen3next) writes the snapshot
  cpy from a raw view of the concat, so the gdn matcher accepts that cpy when
  its source is a 3-column view (qwen4exp already wraps it in a cont).

Default ON (GGML_CUDA_DISABLE_CONV_FUSION=1 is the A/B kill switch).
Bit-identical: fused vs unfused width-probe row0 hashes match exactly
(qwen4exp 268e0673300b7a33, 35B  e97c9e304ce1ca8f) and same-seed greedy text
is identical; width_purity=PASS (worst maxdiff 0) on both.

gfx1151, -b/-ub 8192, -ctk/ctv f16, r=2, no other env:
  qwen4exp IQ4_NL   pp8192 1223.1 -> 1259.9 (+3.0 %)  pp32768 1158.4 -> 1195.6 (+3.2 %)
  qwen35moe 35B Q4  pp8192 2128.1 -> 2265.9 (+6.5 %)  pp32768 1561.9 -> 1672.5 (+7.1 %)

Exported to wip/closing-the-gap/patches/0004.
